{"case_id":"C051","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["missing API entry point","missing post-handshake state","missing output and retry semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["mbedtls_ssl_write","ssl_write_real"],"reason":"S1 changes the public application-data write path so that mbedtls_ssl_write() calls ssl_write_real() directly, but H0 never calls mbedtls_ssl_write() after a successful handshake. Consequently, H0 cannot exercise the changed outgoing-record behavior, including zero/one-byte and maximum-fragment boundary writes or the out_left retry path through mbedtls_ssl_flush_output().","evidence":["In H0, a successful mbedtls_ssl_handshake() is followed only by repeated mbedtls_ssl_read() calls; there is no mbedtls_ssl_write() invocation.","In S1, mbedtls_ssl_write() unconditionally assigns ret = ssl_write_real( ssl, buf, len ), replacing the conditional ssl_write_split() path.","ssl_write_real() contains fuzz-relevant length semantics: len may be zero, stream writes larger than max_len are truncated, and datagram writes return MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_BAD_INPUT_DATA.","ssl_write_real() also has stateful retry behavior when ssl->out_left != 0, calling mbedtls_ssl_flush_output() and requiring repeated calls with the same parameters.","H0's only write-related configuration, mbedtls_ssl_conf_cbc_record_splitting(), is guarded by MBEDTLS_SSL_CBC_RECORD_SPLITTING, which S1 removes from config.h along with that API."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0 with a post-handshake mbedtls_ssl_write() phase using fuzz-derived payloads and lengths, including 0, 1, the negotiated maximum, and over-maximum values; make the send callback capable of partial writes or MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_WANT_WRITE and repeat mbedtls_ssl_write() with identical arguments to exercise out_left flushing semantics."}
